From: ponwrt build fix <build@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mediatek: always provide mtk_soc_wed_ops

The mt76 package on this target is built with -DCONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_SOC_WED
so that mt7915_mmio_wed_init() participates in the build and can attach to
the out-of-tree WED provider.

mtk_wed_ops.c only defines and exports the mtk_soc_wed_ops pointer; it has
no dependency on the MediaTek Ethernet driver or on any other WED object.

However it is currently gated behind CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_SOC_WED, which is
unreachable on ARCH_AIROHA (Kconfig: depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK ||
COMPILE_TEST). modpost therefore reports

  ERROR: modpost: "mtk_soc_wed_ops" [mt7915/mt7915e.ko] undefined!

Build the object unconditionally. A previously succeeding build only worked
because a stale Module.symvers still carried the symbol.

Signed-off-by: ponwrt build fix <build@localhost>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/Makefile
@@ -9,5 +9,5 @@
 ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS
 mtk_eth-$(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_SOC_WED) += mtk_wed_debugfs.o
 endif
-obj-$(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_SOC_WED) += mtk_wed_ops.o
+obj-y += mtk_wed_ops.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_NET_MEDIATEK_STAR_EMAC) += mtk_star_emac.o
